# BPI-R4 image artifacts.  The device profile only references the bootloader pieces
# through ARTIFACT/..., and ARTIFACT/... adds no package dependency, while the
# profile's DEVICE_PACKAGES (identical to upstream) carry no U-Boot or ATF packages
# either.  So nothing selected them, and target/linux install died with
#
#   cat: .../staging_dir/.../image/mt7988-emmc-comb-bl2.img: No such file or directory
#   make[5]: *** [Makefile:132: ...-emmc-preloader.bin] Error 1
#
# Each U-Boot variant depends on the ATF variant that produces its bl2 (the emmc
# package on trusted-firmware-a-mt7988-emmc-comb, snand on
# trusted-firmware-a-mt7988-spim-nand-ubi-comb, sdmmc on
# trusted-firmware-a-mt7988-sdmmc-comb), so selecting the three U-Boot packages
# pulls the ATF in as well.  The trusted-firmware-a lines are listed explicitly
# too: they are what actually lands in staging_dir/.../image/, and a name that does
# not exist is dropped by make defconfig without a word.
#
# The U-Boot symbol really is u-boot-<variant>, not uboot-mediatek-<variant>:
# uboot-mediatek only names the source package (PKG_NAME at the top of its
# Makefile), while the binary packages come from
# "define Package/u-boot-$(1)" / "$(call BuildPackage,u-boot-$(type))" in
# Build/U-Boot/Target, with $(1) being the "define U-Boot/<name>" suffix.
CONFIG_PACKAGE_u-boot-mt7988_bananapi_bpi-r4-emmc=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_u-boot-mt7988_bananapi_bpi-r4-snand=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_u-boot-mt7988_bananapi_bpi-r4-sdmmc=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_trusted-firmware-a-mt7988-emmc-comb=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_trusted-firmware-a-mt7988-spim-nand-ubi-comb=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_trusted-firmware-a-mt7988-sdmmc-comb=y
